  SWEEP of every `inspect.getsource(<named function>)` assertion we own (BOSS's ask). Four sites.
  Method: mutate mergegate.py in a scratch mirror and measure which mutations each assertion
  catches — not read them and reason. THREE OF FOUR WERE ALREADY BLIND, measured, not suspected:
  comment the wiring out and leave the original text as a trailing comment, and all three files
  stayed GREEN. getsource cannot tell live code from a commented-out corpse; what it proves is that
  a string is present in a file.
