  and a defect in our own parsing printed the same `verdict=NONE FOUND (fail-closed)`, and those two
  demand opposite responses: wait vs look.
  A wall with no reset time says the time was not given rather than inventing one.
  RETRY: the call is never SKIPPED while walled — the wall costs about a second to discover and may
  have lifted, whereas a skip decides on stale information. Capped at ONE retry, and only for the
  wall: a parse error or an empty answer is not made truer by asking again.
  Test: dispatcher/tests/test_codexwall.py — 22 checks over the REAL 22:08 .codex.txt from gate
  83676 (copied to fixtures, never read live), including the control that an approving review is
  untouched, that an unreadable-but-present review is NOT dressed up as an outage, that the walled
  output can never be read as an approval, and an END-TO-END run of the gate asserting the rendered
  .md row and exactly two reviewer calls. Verified failing (AttributeError) against a94b178f.

