temp git checkout with `_run_proofs` forced to raise the actual FileNotFoundError, and requires the
.md to exist, its verdict to be FAIL, the proofs row to name the exception, the stamp block to be
present, and a GATE_FAIL event to have been emitted naming the item. Everything that needs the world
is stubbed EXCEPT the thing under test.
This also settles the question I had staged for BOSS about a crash-path .md: it is not needed. The
gate no longer crashes, so "a .md exists" still means "a gate ran to completion" — the invariant is
kept rather than weakened, which is the better answer than the one I proposed.

(2) `resolve_venv(scratch, wt)` makes the venv source an explicit, RECORDED decision instead of
"whatever the lane happened to have":
  lane   — the lane's own venv, still preferred: it is the one the executor used.
  trunk  — trunk's venv, but ONLY when the candidate's dependency spec (platform/pyproject.toml +
           platform/uv.lock) is byte-identical to trunk's. The row then reads
           `venv=trunk (pyproject.toml + uv.lock identical, <digest>)`.
  refusal— no usable venv: a NOT RUN row naming the lane, the digests when they differ, and why a
           venv built for other dependencies would make any green here meaningless.
