## 2026-09-06 21:39 — mergegate.py: a missing binary killed a whole gate (66276)
md5 1554cbf5 -> 6a0165a7. Two fixes; a third (a crash-path gate file) is staged pending BOSS.

Gate 66276 (B.010.ci-required-guard-residuals) exited rc=1 with NO gate file although Codex had run
and its .codex.txt existed. Cause, from the .out (the whole file is one traceback): the lane
worktree `voicepod-lane-ci-guard-residuals` has no `platform/.venv`, so run_proofs' symlink loop
(`if os.path.exists(src)`) made none, the provenance probe exec'd an interpreter that does not
exist, and subprocess raised FileNotFoundError. `sh()` did not catch it, so it propagated out of
run_proofs and out of main — killing the gate after the box, the reviewers and the sweep had all
been paid for and BEFORE render_gate_md().

What the crash cost, and what it did NOT: no verdict (rc=1 from an uncaught exception is not a FAIL,
and there is no GATE_ event for that item), no proof measurement at all — it died before the first
test — and no stamp. The box lock was NOT left held and the scratch worktree was removed: run_proofs'
finally ran before the exception propagated. Verified, not assumed. BOSS was about to write a
verdict from the .codex.txt alone; that would have recorded a FAIL whose proof row never existed.

1. `sh()` catches OSError and returns (127, the message). Every caller already handles a non-zero
   rc; none of them can handle an exception. A missing binary is a MEASUREMENT — "the interpreter is
   not there" — and 127 is the shell's own word for it. A real non-zero exit is still reported as
   itself (asserted, so 127 cannot become a catch-all that hides a genuine 3).
2. run_proofs checks for the venv before the probe and records a named FAIL naming the LANE, what to
   do about it, and — the part that matters for anyone reading the row later — that NO test was
   executed, so no result is implied.

Calibration tests/test_missingvenv.py, 10/10, hermetic: sh() on a missing binary returns 127 with
the error named; a working command and a genuine exit 3 are unaffected; the missing-venv row is a
FAIL that names the lane, the remedy and the absence of any test result; and the row's text is
asserted to be the one actually shipped in run_proofs rather than a copy in the test.

