## 2026-09-06 21:22 — dispatcher.py: a pending row can be about work that already LANDED
md5 cf16a0d8 -> fd58bbe9. Rerun: `./dispatcherctl.sh selftest`.

21:13 (BOSS): CODEX-1's 02:40 REPORT_READY sat on the board eleven hours after its artifact had
LANDED (capped) on trunk at 18dea63d, and a worker was dispatched from it. A pending row records
that an executor said something; nothing ever re-read it against the world.

`tag_stale()` resolves each pending row to its queue item, then asks two independent sources: the
item's own status (landed/merged/done) and its artifact's ledger block (LANDED/MERGED). Either one
tags the row `[STALE — <item> is MERGED at <sha> (<time>)]` on the board line, records the reason on
the row itself, and emits ONE PENDING_STALE per row per reason. It does NOT prune: the row may still
carry a question only BOSS can close, so the tag says so and BOSS clears it. Rows created from now
on carry their item id (both the opencode and the Codex creation sites), so the recovery path below
is only needed for rows that predate this.

A DEFECT CAUGHT IN CALIBRATION, worth keeping in mind for anything that matches ids in strings: the
first version recovered a row's item by testing whether any queue id appears in the msg_id. That
matched the two-character item `Q2` inside `msg_072017ec1001VBvMlAe6TX60Q2` and tagged EXEC-E's LIVE
ERROR row as finished work. A cross-check that mis-identifies its subject is worse than none — it
retires the wrong row. Now: only a Codex log filename (`*.log`, where the item id genuinely IS part
of the name) is matched, ids under 6 characters are ignored, and the longest match wins so
`B.010.ci-required-green` cannot lose to a prefix of itself. The must-pass that all three ERROR rows
stay untagged is what caught it and is kept.

`dispatcherctl.sh status` prints `!! <reason>` under any stale row.
Calibration tests/test_stalerow.py, 17/17, against the recorded pending.json + queue.json: three
assertions are on the fixture (the CODEX-1 row is a REPORT_READY, it carries no item field, its item
really is finished), and the must-passes are that BUILT/HELD artifacts stay untagged, unfinished
rows stay untagged, an unresolvable row is left alone rather than guessed at, and nothing is pruned.

