2026-09-07 04:13  agy packer: whole product files where they fit; and an escalation that lied.
  gatereview2.py e253962d -> eee196c5   mergegate.py ffb25b07 -> 5019d8dc
  autogate.py a54ac3d3 -> f115ec15
  NEW tests/test_packwhole.py 26e9ce4c; amended test_agydirs fed6da19, test_agynoreview 1f640bd9,
  test_autogate 411e2976; run_all 413d668c; README 3949d70e. Suite rc 0.

  PACKER (owner directive via BOSS, approved on measurement). Measured first on 9 real candidates,
  133 product files, their live worktrees: packing every product file WHOLE costs a median 6.6x its
  hunks — median 811k against a 180k budget, 8 of 9 candidates over — so that version was REJECTED.
  Upgrading to whole files only where they FIT shows 52% of product files in full (69/133), keeps
  every candidate inside budget (median 168,752, max 179,735), and leaves the rest exactly the hunks
  they had. That is what shipped.
  Today's packing runs unchanged first; the upgrade pass then swaps stanzas already IN the pack,
  cheapest upgrade first, so a file that could not be fitted as a hunk cannot appear and nothing that
  fits today is lost. With no spare budget the pack is BYTE-IDENTICAL to today (a must-bite).
  BOSS's two conditions, both required: a whole file is labelled `===== FULL FILE (not a diff) =====`
  with an end marker and its diff stanza removed, because a reviewer reading a full file as a diff
  reports unchanged lines as findings and BOSS would hold a lane on a defect that does not exist;
  and the packed set is written per gate to gates/<item>.packed.txt (FULL / hunk / TAIL / NONE with
  bytes), which is what separates "the reviewer missed it" from "the reviewer never saw it".
  Whole files are read from the CANDIDATE SHA, not the working tree: the tree can move under a
  running gate, and a reviewer shown a file the gate did not measure produces findings about code
  that is not in the candidate.
