THE CHECKPOINT REPORTER — `dispatcherctl.sh checkpoint [since-sha]`, read-only, stdout.

BOSS asked for the night's state generated from evidence rather than from memory, in five sections:
merged tonight (with Rule 3 marked per merge), held/in rework, in flight, the item-3 gate split, and
what is open for the owner. Two rules governed it: print "not measured" where a source does not
carry a fact — never an inferred value and never a blank, which reads as zero — and be re-runnable,
so a 09:00 run shows the same shape with newer numbers.

What it reads: test-logs/driver/queue.json, test-logs/driver/events.log, and `git log --merges
<since>..plan010/rebuild` in voice-pod. It writes nothing and takes no lock, so it is safe beside a
live gate. plans/EXECUTION_LEDGER.md is NOT read: there is no copy at the CN root (only inside lane
worktrees), and a report that silently substituted one lane's ledger for the program's would be
exactly the inferred value the first rule forbids.

Rule 3 is READ, never inferred: a merge is LANDED only where the merge commit itself says so, and
"MERGED" is reported as the absence of a non-builder audit and a named passing test on the merged
tree rather than as completion. Inferring LANDED from an approve verdict is one of the mutations.

Two things the build itself found:
  * `def merged_section(since=SINCE)` bound the default AT DEFINITION, so `checkpoint.py <sha>` set
    the global and changed nothing — the report used 0dbc9ae1 whatever the caller asked. The
    hermetic test points the base at its own temp repo and got an empty section 1. A live run could
    not have shown this: the live default is correct.
  * Section 4 asked for GATE_PASS:GATE_FAIL and measures 0:9 before / 0:8 after — a column of zeros
    that says nothing, because the overall verdict is the AND of every check and a --no-box gate
    scores proofs=FAIL by construction. So the same events are also split on the two components the
    event text carries. Codex adversarial review is 0:9 before the rules and 7:1 after. That is the
    item-3 signal, and the headline verdict hides it.

The test asserts on the GENERATED MARKDOWN, not on helper return values, because the document is
what BOSS and the owner read. Mutations, each redding its own assertion, control clean:
  unmeasured gates swept into the "before" cell        1 red
  not-measured becomes a blank cell                    5 reds (see below)
  LANDED inferred from an approve verdict              1 red
