A CHECK THAT COULD NOT RUN IS NOT A CHECK THAT FAILED.

BOSS, 2026-09-07, out of the checkpoint reporter's own finding: `proofs=FAIL` on a --no-box gate is
wrong reporting and has been miscolouring every gate of the night. It also made his metric
unmovable — the overall verdict is the AND of every row, so GATE_PASS:GATE_FAIL sat at 0:9 and 0:8
while the reviewer signal underneath went 0:9 to 7:1.

rec() takes a third state: True PASS, False FAIL, None NOT RUN, which never touches state["ok"].
  verdict     FAIL (x not run) | INCOMPLETE (x not run) | PASS — PASS only when everything ran
  event kind  GATE_PASS only when everything ran and passed; new GATE_INCOMPLETE otherwise
  exit code   0 PASS, 1 FAIL, 3 INCOMPLETE — a shell `rc == 0` must not read unrun as success
  autopilot   never merges an INCOMPLETE gate; emits MERGE_SKIPPED naming what did not run
  autogate    parses the third status; failed_rows() no longer sweeps it in; INCOMPLETE escalates
  checkpoint  an INCOMPLETE column in the headline, a did-not-run column in each component split

FOUR rows converted and no more: --no-box, --no-codex, box busy > 60 min, census-occupied. The Codex
WALL and 1800s-timeout rows stay FAIL: fail-CLOSED there is a standing BOSS ruling about the
reviewer, and overturning it unasked is not this session's call. Flagged to BOSS as the obvious next
one — the wall row already says "NO review was performed... a reviewer outage, not a finding".

Verdict word: BOSS offered "PASS (proofs not run)" as acceptable; INCOMPLETE is the stronger of the
two he named and is what shipped. A reader skims the first word and so does every counter.

A REAL BUG fell out of it. dispatcher.py passes --no-box to EVERY box-free item, so an item with no
declared .py proofs recorded `proofs: FAIL — not run` and COULD NEVER GATE ANYTHING BUT FAIL,
however green its portal row was. Not applicable and did not run are now different: a box-free item
is measured by its own portal row; only declared .py proofs nobody ran hold the verdict.

Mutations (each reds its own assertions; behaviour-preserving control 0):
