over budget. Recounted here independently before building on it: sums identical, and MAX_DIFF really
is 180,000, so his corrected table stands.

The signal he asked for: occupancy in the gate row AND in the input header above the verdict, plus a
loud line at >=90% — nothing was lost from THIS review, the next commit starts dropping files, check
the coverage count before trusting the verdict, split the candidate. backfills-r2 is at 99.7% on the
lane carrying a ruled [high]. Control: a 4% pack is quiet, or a warning on every gate is a warning
on none. occupancy() is ONE function with ONE test precisely because the repeated-arithmetic version
is what caught him.

`:.0f` printed 99.7% as "100% of budget", which reads as AT the limit — the one number a reader acts
on differently. pct() floors: 99% while a byte remains, 100% only when full.

(3) THE ANSWERED EVENT NAMES A SURVIVING FEED HOLD. BOSS's ruling: `answer` must NOT clear a feed
hold — a question is closed by an answer, a pause is closed by a judgement that the executor is fit
to continue, and a verb that silently resumes feeding is a bigger surprise than one that does not.
But an un-parked row whose executor is still held reads as "back to work", so the event now says the
