  the QUESTION pending row and emitted ANSWERED. The record said an executor had been told something
  nobody told it.
  - the answer path now checks the result; both roads (False and a raise) end in the same refusal:
    row STILL PARKED, QUESTION still pending, no answered_at, ANSWER_FAILED + escalation.
  - post_prompt records WHY on the instance (_last_post_error). The reason existed and went only to
    the log, so the event BOSS reads had to be vague about the one thing he needed.
  - OBSERVE-ONLY is reported as a held actuator, not a delivery failure — otherwise the switch loses
    answers AND sends BOSS hunting for a network fault that does not exist.
  TESTS, through the REAL helper with http broken underneath it (Plan 003 §8). The old failure test
  used a stub that RAISES, which the real helper never does — a test of a path the product cannot
  take, and the reason the defect survived.
  THE HARNESS WAS PART OF THE DEFECT: the default stub was `lambda sid, text: posted.append(...)`,
  which returns None, i.e. it modelled a FAILED post while every check read it as success. Harmless
  only for as long as the code ignored the result — the moment the fix honoured the contract, twelve
  green tests turned red at once. Stubs now return True.
  Mutation-scored, restores verified: reverting the CALL SITE (`if not delivered:` -> `if False:`)
  CAUGHT; dropping the recorded reason CAUGHT.
  INVENTORIED, NOT FIXED: 8 call sites still drop post_prompt's result (lines 1975, 2025, 2048,
